8 | 0.0686 | 0.0647 |\\\\n-| 256 | 0.0559 | 0.0666 | 0.0371 | 0.0466 | 0.1004 | 0.0915 |\\\\n-| 1024 | 0.1730 | 0.1849 | 0.0668 | 0.0736 | 0.2486 | 0.2497 |\\\\n-\\\\n-All values are milliseconds. CD3 reduces isolated H2D by 40.8%, 30.9%, 16.1%,\\\\n-and 6.4%, and isolated resident decode by 32.5%, 35.9%, 20.4%, and 9.2% at\\\\n-the four sizes. The complete one-stream call is 11.8%, 6.0%, and 9.7% slower\\\\n-at N=8/64/256 and tied at N=1024. P4Flat's C++ `decode_layer_prep` has lower\\\\n-fixed preparation/dispatch cost; at small N this outweighs CD3's faster copy\\\\n-and kernel in the complete-call timing.\\\\n+| 8 | 0.0166 | 0.0279 | 0.0281 | 0.0455 | 0.0432 | 0.0622 |\\\\n+| 64 | 0.0261 | 0.0363 | 0.0282 | 0.0439 | 0.0413 | 0.0645 |\\\\n+| 256 | 0.0556 | 0.0670 | 0.0356 | 0.0472 | 0.0791 | 0.0918 |\\\\n+| 1024 | 0.1669 | 0.1829 | 0.0687 | 0.0745 | 0.2230 | 0.2471 |\\\\n+\\\\n+All values are milliseconds from the final saved run. CD3 reduces the\\\\n+complete one-stream call by 30.6%, 36.0%, 13.8%, and 9.8% at the four sizes.\\\\n+The fixed dispatch gap was removed by publishing the canonical active set once\\\\n+per forward, caching the generation-safe decode plan, and dispatching the\\\\n+native paired decoder on an explicit CUDA stream. Every case was bit-exact.\\\\n@@\\\\n reproduced H2D/decode/total = 0.229/0.081/0.300 ms, matching the old\\\\n 0.232/0.082/0.302 ms. Thus that ordering was a real result for the old P4Flat\\\\n configuration, but it is not the correct comparison against current P4Flat.\\\\n+\\\\n+The final raw output is stored in `kv_standalone_final_20260901.log` beside\\\\n+this report. The script's `cpu_encode` field is one setup call in a fresh\\\\n+process and is not used as the production CPU-encoder comparison; section 4.2\\\\n+uses the dedicated steady-state encoder benchmark.\\\\n@@\\\\n The 1856 versus 1330 cutoff should not be presented as a 39.5% direct\\\\n performance speedup: it says that CD3 remains worth decoding over a 526-token\\\\n wider range under this residency/fabric/model combination.\\\\n@@\\\\n serving work masks the per-layer difference. This is a CD3 route ablation, not\\\\n a CD3-versus-P4Flat end-to-end result.\\\\n+\\\\n+### 8.1 Final full-serving comparison\\\\n+\\\\n+The final comparison used `scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh` with\\\\n+`cao-p4flat-fused-kvcomp,cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp`, batch sizes 64 and 128, input\\\\n+length 1020, generation length 129, and one repeat. Both methods used CPU\\\\n+weight encode, CPU KV encode, GPU fused/standalone weight decode according to\\\\n+their production route, and compressed KV H2D+GPU decode. Encode setup is not\\\\n+included in TTFT/TPOT. The GPU and hugepage state was clean at each method\\\\n+boundary.\\\\n+\\\\n+| Batch | P4 TTFT median | CD3 TTFT median | P4 TPOT median | CD3 TPOT median | CD3 TPOT change |\\\\n+|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\\\n+| 64 | 1846.63 ms | 1838.72 ms | 124.66 ms | 114.51 ms | 8.14% faster |\\\\n+| 128 | 337.96 ms | 338.02 ms | 180.59 ms | 166.64 ms | 7.72% faster |\\\\n+\\\\n+TPOT means were 129.95 versus 120.19 ms at batch 64 (7.51% faster) and\\\\n+196.80 versus 187.12 ms at batch 128 (4.92% faster). These are whole-engine\\\\n+results, so they include weight routing, attention, scheduling, KV transport,\\\\n+KV decode, and CPU compression contention rather than isolating one codec\\\\n+kernel.\\\\n+\\\\n+For a 16-layer KV-only pipeline, CD3's H2D/decode overlap reduced its own\\\\n+makespan by 30.3% at N=256 and 25.8% at N=1024. Against P4Flat's best measured\\\\n+setting, CD3 was 46.7%, 20.8%, and 1.0% faster at N=64/256/1024. The production\\\\n+threshold keeps N<256 on one stream because two-stream event overhead exceeds\\\\n+overlap benefit there.\\\\n@@\\\\n - Cached block/slot GPU metadata and one native paired K/V decode dispatch.\\\\n-- Active-set identity/content caching with generation-safe invalidation.\\\\n+- The loader publishes the canonical active set once per forward; per-layer\\\\n+  decoding then uses identity/version checks with generation-safe invalidation\\\\n+  instead of repeating a NumPy content comparison 80 times.\\\\n - Dense steady-state plans that skip filtering, sorting, and contiguous-run\\\\n   reconstruction.\\\\n+- Explicit-stream native decode dispatch and a two-slot compressed-blob HBM\\\\n+  ring overlap layer L+1 H2D with layer L decode for N>=256. Smaller restores\\\\n+  stay on one stream to avoid fixed event/stream overhead.\\\\n+- The KV memory planner accounts for CD3's fixed compressed row and reserves\\\\n+  one resident partial-tail row per request, preventing host over-allocation\\\\n+  and preserving full-block correctness.\\\\n@@\\\\n-- The current 27-file implementation is stored as one checksum-verified,\\\\n-  idempotent HFS startup patch.\\\\n+- The current implementation is stored in checksum-verified, idempotent HFS\\\\n+  startup patches for tiered-serve and its two required vLLM integration\\\\n+  points.\\\\n@@\\\\n - Direct-to-persistent Packed20 CPU packing: 3--6% slower at medium/large N.\\\\n - Broad SVE2 rewrites: slower; only targeted predicate counting was retained.\\\\n+- Reducing the fixed KV exception capacity from 768 to 384 saved bytes on the\\\\n+  sampled Llama KV cache, but was not retained: the observed maximum is not a\\\\n+  correctness bound, and there is no overflow-safe variable-row fallback.\\\\n@@\\\\n | KV 2-D/direct-cache kernel | Tiered-serve `[16,8,128]` KV layout fit | Validate block size, head count/head dimension, row strides, and cache index mapping |\\\\n+| KV split threshold 256 | GH200 transfer/launch fit | Re-sweep the serial/two-stream crossover; correctness is independent of the value |\\\\n+| Fixed exception capacity 768 | Workload safety bound | Profile the target KV exception tail; do not reduce it without an overflow-safe fallback |\\\\n | H2D savings | GH200 unified Grace/LPDDR/HBM fabric fit | Re-measure on PCIe, NVLink, B200, or GB200; byte savi